From 3020c9713f7290db1e52ae4c1676d95109b04850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:27:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add multi-user auth: User/Patient split, JWT cookie
 sessions, open registration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every tester now gets their own account instead of the app assuming one
implicit patient. A new User table holds login credentials, 1:1-linked to the
existing Patient (clinical profile) table via patients.user_id — every
already-existing patient_id-scoped table needed no new column, only a
trustworthy per-request source for "whose data is this" to replace
`session.query(Patient).first()`.

- app/database/models.py: User model, patients.user_id column, idempotent
  _ensure_columns() migration run on every startup.
- app/auth/security.py: PBKDF2-SHA256 password hashing (600k iterations),
  HS256 JWT (stdlib PyJWT, no new crypto dependency).
- app/auth/dependencies.py: get_current_user / get_current_patient_id read
  the session from an httpOnly cookie only; require_admin gates the
  Garmin/Withings/Calendar integrations (see next commit); a simple in-memory
  rate limiter guards /register and /login.
- app/api/auth.py: register (open, email+password, explicit GDPR consent,
  creates the user's own empty Patient row) / login / logout / me.
- app/main.py: registers the auth router, flips CORS allow_credentials to
  True (needed for the cookie to ride cross-origin fetch calls), and drops
  the old create_default_patient() bootstrap — patients are created at
  registration now, one per user.
- scripts/migrate_multi_user.py: one-time script to link the existing
  production Patient row (and its previously-unowned Document rows) to a new
  admin account. Must be run once before testers register, per its docstring.

Household/family grouping is deliberately out of scope for this pass (see
claude/prompt-multi-profil-rodina.md in the MedicalAI project) — every
account is fully independent.
