From ec59bf89b5916b09c94746766d6584ccd6a0bd39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:27:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Thread patient_id through analysis, ML, RAG and the chat
 tool layer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Everything the dashboard, chat and predictions read from was either an
unscoped query (session.query(Patient).first()) or a process-wide cache —
both fine with one implicit patient, both a cross-tenant leak with more than
one:

- app/analysis/sources.py: every loader now takes patient_id and filters by
  it.
- app/analysis/health_metrics.py, trend_analyzer.py: analyzers now take
  patient_id at construction. TrendAnalyzer's data cache became
  Dict[patient_id, DataFrame] instead of one shared slot — without this, one
  patient's cached frame could answer another patient's request for up to
  the 300s TTL. Legacy extracted_data_*.json loading (predates the database,
  carries no patient_id of its own) is dropped rather than attributed to
  every patient.
- app/rag/retriever.py: the BM25 index cache became the same
  Dict[patient_id, ...] shape, for the same reason; index_document,
  document_inventory and search all take patient_id and filter Document
  queries by it.
- app/ml/risk_predictor.py: RiskPredictor takes patient_id and builds its own
  TrendAnalyzer(patient_id) instead of a bare TrendAnalyzer().
- app/analysis/chat_context.py, app/chat_tools.py: build_health_context and
  every tool handler take patient_id from the authenticated request, never
  from model/tool input — a tool schema that let the model pass its own
  patient_id would turn "look up my history" into a parameter an
  attacker-controlled prompt could redirect at someone else's data.

Tests updated for the new signatures and per-patient cache shape, plus a new
cross-patient case in test_rag.py (two patients' documents must never answer
each other's search).
